From ffddb3fc6e316e0b290aafcc9ed2e87273d05625 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: go-while <go-while@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:06:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] tests/overview: Close Xref searches before testing
 cancellation

Release every search handle after checking its article. Otherwise the
test retains references to the mapped group data throughout the later
cancellation checks.

tradindexed_cancel reopens its cached data files so cancelled entries
are no longer visible on OpenBSD, but leaked search references keep the
old mappings alive. Close those references rather than changing the
production cancellation path to accommodate a leaking test.

Co-Authored-By: GPT-6.1 Sol <noreply@openai.com>
---
 tests/overview/xref-t.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/overview/xref-t.c b/tests/overview/xref-t.c
index 169792f8c..328f40e51 100644
--- a/tests/overview/xref-t.c
+++ b/tests/overview/xref-t.c
@@ -158,6 +158,10 @@ overview_load(int n, const char *data, struct overview *overview)
                 ok_int(n++, strlen(start) + (result - article.overview) + 2,
                        article.overlen);
             }
+            /* Release the search's reference to the mapped data so a later
+             * cancellation can close and reopen it, as OpenBSD requires. */
+            if (search != NULL)
+                overview_search_close(overview, search);
         }
     }
     fclose(overdata);
